<title>USA: Tietmeyer repeats need for strong dollar.</title>
<headline>Tietmeyer repeats need for strong dollar.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Bundesbank President Hans Tietmeyer on Sunday repeated his assertion that he favored a strong dollar now and into the future.</p>
<p>&quot;I hope very much the dollar will remain strong now and in the upcoming months and years,&quot; he told reporters during the annual IMF/World Bank annual meeting.</p>
<p>At the same time, he said the mark was not weak, taking the view that it had been overvalued in the past year but that the correction was now complete.</p>
<p>&quot;So all in all I expect relatively calm exchange rate developments in the upcoming months,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>He also said the German money supply was a little bit above its targets and &quot;I hope it will come down and more in line with the targets.&quot;</p>
</text>
